<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Daily recomputation of the family gate: R0 at today's ledger bucket size.  It never touches the
      venue and it changes no book, but it is NOT read-only - every PASS/FAIL appends a `family_gate`
      row to governance/verdicts.jsonl, which is the point of running it.

      Why it exists.  The mechanism has been complete since 2026-09-09 and had no caller: nothing in
      deploy/ ran it, so the reading existed only when somebody typed the command.  Same shape as the
      forward-board plist that shipped uninstalled on 2026-09-17 - a rule with no alarm clock.

      Baseline on the day it was added (2026-09-19): tsmom PASS with 0.0158 of headroom, down from
      0.0426 at adoption as N went 242 -> 305; flow UNREADABLE.  The curve is the reason for the job.

      Runs at 02:30 local, after the forward board at 02:00 - both read reports/research/.

      Install (operator action):
        cp deploy/com.beidou.governance-gate.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
        launchctl load -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.beidou.governance-gate.plist
    -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.beidou.governance-gate</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/maguannan/beidou/deploy/run_governance_gate.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/maguannan/beidou</string>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>2</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/maguannan/Library/Application Support/beidou/governance-gate.stdout.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/maguannan/Library/Application Support/beidou/governance-gate.stderr.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
